            <div class="chapter-content">
                <p class="story">By an abandoned pool reclaimed by moss and grass, a lone astronaut sits—homesick, unsure. The real insight: you realize you're not alone in feeling alone. Sometimes the most profound connection comes from recognizing shared struggle.</p>
                <p class="practice"><strong>Practice: Name it to tame it</strong> <br> Whisper one word for what you feel. Place a hand on your chest; say aloud: <strong>"This is hard, but others feel this too."</strong> Many find that simply naming an emotion can help reduce its intensity—a concept often referred to as "affect labeling."</p>
            </div>
        </article>

