            <div class="chapter-content">
                <p class="story">A purple-leafed canopy opens; the falls thunder and soothe. Here's the paradox: release doesn't require permission—only patience and time. The water doesn't force its way down; it simply follows the path of least resistance.</p>
                <div class="practice">
                    <strong>Practice: RAIN for Release</strong>
                    <ul class="practice-list">
                        <li><strong>Recognize</strong> one stress (name it specifically) without getting lost in the feeling.</li>
                        <li><strong>Allow</strong> it without resistance, judgment, or trying to change it.</li>
                        <li><strong>Investigate</strong> with kindness (where do you feel it in your body?)</li>
                        <li><strong>Nurture</strong> with a gentle phrase ("I will be kind to myself today.")</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.8em; opacity: 0.8; line-height: 1.4; text-wrap: pretty;">
